 education vesemir explains a bit  of the history behind karamorin and  witcher's abilities he tells her about  fighting and living through the attack  on caremorin in which humans and magic  mutated monsters assault the stronghold  in an attempt to eliminate the witchers  we also see the massive tree in the  middle of karamorin's hall where the  medallions of fallen witchers hang  outside of karamorin's keep bones of  humans and monsters still litter the  ground  including a massive skeleton that looks  like it could very well be from the  mutated griffon that attacks vesimir in  nightmare of the wolf  in the episode 2 scenes that are not set  at caramorn we follow a beat up and  broken down yennefer who is captured by  nilfgaard forces after the battle of  saturn hill she reunites with former  classmate frangilla a sorceress on the  side of nilfgaard she also meets with  francesca an elven mage who is a leader  among her people the three mages enter  some ancient ruins where they eventually  find an illuminated straw house that  begins to move on spindly legs inside  each of them meets a version of the  depthless mother a character created for  the series who serves as a mysterious  antagonist throughout season 2. while  this storyline is not part of the books  the house on stilted legs and the traits  of the deathless mother parallel  elements from the witcher 3 wild hunt  video game the house in particular is  reminiscent of the slavic legend of baba  yaga a mythological character who lives  in a straw cabin that roams around on  chicken legs in the witcher 3 the trio  of witches known as the crones are  loosely based on the tales of baba yaga  as well the deathless mother is also a  bit reminiscent of baba yaga as she is  shown shape-shifting into different  people based on which mage she is  interacting with while the witcher  series on netflix is based on the  stories and characters from the books  both seasons still include subtle nods  to the wildly popular video games season  2's second episode titled caremorin is  all about series education and training  there in one scene vesemir gives siri a  little tour of kare morin's vault which  prominently features weapons and armor  from past witchers the scene focuses on  two gleaming swords which dedicated fans  might recognize from the witcher 3 wild  hunt video game the top sword is the  viper sword a silver sword recognizable  by the snake on the pommel and its  unique bolt-shaped cross guard the  bottom blade is steel and belongs to  geralt in the witcher games witchers  typically carry two swords a steal one  for fighting non-magical beings and one  coated in silver to slay monsters  besides geralt yaskir the bard is one of  the most popular characters in the  witcher series oh aren't you just the  cutest  most  terrifying thing i've ever seen in my  entire life run away run away girl in  season one geralt and yaskir part ways  after an explosive argument that sees  geralt blaming the bard for all of his  recent woes  however yaskir isn't doing so bad in  season two as he has developed a new  look and sound that hearkened back to  his portrayal in the books and games  in these scenes yaskar is also sporting  longer hair an unshaven face and new  attire that is much more in line with  what he wore in the books and games  along with a purple-hued leather coat  one brief scene shows him crooning while  wearing a hat with an egret feather in  it bringing back one of his most  memorable accessories  the witcher second season is largely a  grim affair but there are some moments  of levity thanks to the musical stylings  and commentary by yeskir the bard when  we first see yas gear in episode 4 he's  belting out his newest ballad an epic  breakup song with the hook burn butcher  burn it's angsty emotional and  hilariously recaps some of season 1's  adventures with the witcher from  yaskir's perspective it may not be as  catchy as toss a coin but it brings some  comedic relief to the season one  memorable scene shows a man telling yes  gear that his niece is a big fan of his  work but he also has a few pointed  critiques for one of yesgear's  a bit complicated it took me to the  fourth verse to understand their  different timelines  this is of course a hilarious and  self-aware nod to the convoluted  timelines of season one the witcher  creators have been upfront about changes  to the structure of the show for this  season showrunner lauren schmidt  hissrick participated in an ask me  anything on reddit in 2020 where she  detailed how season 2 would be much less  confusing for those who were thrown off  by season 1. second season geralt grunts  much less than he did in season 1. a  trait the witcher himself henry cavill  said he pushed hard to change per  gizmodo that doesn't stop yes gear from  hilariously poking fun at geralt's grunt  in season 2 saying that geralt's grunts  and he makes a song we wonder how geralt  would feel about that  doesn't rhyme  by the middle of season 2 you'll notice  geralt has fashioned himself some shiny  new armor this new armor made out of  thick plates and leather is both  imposing and allows geralt more  flexibility while fighting monsters in  addition the new armor also symbolizes a  key evolution in geralt's character and  philosophy in a release from netflix  cavil said he had a big hand in  redesigning the witcher's new armor  which made it easier for him to move  around and fight throughout the creation  of both seasons cavill has been open  about his love for the witcher franchise  the books games and show and about his  influences on making changes to geralt's  look and character through all 16  episodes geralt's new armor isn't just  about the character's mobility in the  same release cavill explained that this  new armor symbolizes geralt's comfort in  remaining in one place for a longer  period of time  typically geralt is a loner on the move  with no opportunities to fashion new  armor however the time he spends in  karamorin with siri eskel and lambert  shows his belief in the safety of the  witcher stronghold and his trust in his  fellow monster hunters  in episode six titled dear friend a very  pregnant francesca walks with frangilla  in the gardens of sintra the two  sorcerers have become friends and  clearly care for one another but have  very different goals  while frangela serves nilfgaard and the  mysterious white flame francesca's chief  concern is the safety of her unborn  child and her people the elves while the  two walk francesca stops to bring some  white roses back to life and picks a few  for her baby's bassinet she also tells  frangilla about discovering her magical  powers following the death of her mother  with whom she loved to pick flowers in  the book blood of elves white roses are  symbols of the elven heroine elerin also  called the white rose of cherowin arylan  is best known for leading a last  desperate battle against the humans in  the books white roses still grow at the  ruins of sherwood and francesca's  revitalization of the flowers is a small  nod to elerin's sacrifice  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies and tv shows are  coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

